<title>DUBAI: UAE's Al-Dhafra Insurance raises 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>UAE's Al-Dhafra Insurance raises 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(million dirhams unless stated, rounded)</p>
<p>    Total dividend		  10.00   vs	8.16</p>
<p>    Net profit			23.82   vs     22.98</p>
<p>    Net underwriting income     25.54   vs     24.04</p>
<p>    Gross premiums written     113.05   vs    113.87</p>
<p>    Investment income		7.52   vs	7.55</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item	     1.03   vs	 nil</p>
<p>Full name: Al-Dhafra Insurance Company PSC</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said a provision of 6.43 million dirhams was established at end-1994 against term deposits with the failed Bank of Credit and Commerce International. In December 1996, the company received 1.03 million dirhams from the BCCI liquidators -- its first interim liquidation settlement.</p>
<p>($1=3.67 dirhams)</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714-607-1219</p>
